Hi,

On Sat, 30 Jul 2022 15:12:51 -0400
Brian Lunergan <ff809 at ncf.ca> wrote:
> Pulled in the most recent edition of Rkward. Running it on Linux Mint
> 20.3 under the Cinnamon DTE. Everything seems okay but the config
> window comes up too large for the screen on my laptop and will not
> cooperate when I try to make it smaller. Even with the panel across
> the bottom hidden the cancel and save buttons are not viewable or
> accessible. Curiously, even the edition of Kate I pulled in has the
> same issue.
> 
> Any ideas for a solution or even just a work-around?

as for a workaround, most window managers on Linux allow to move a
window by holding Alt, the clicking anywhere in the window and
dragging. This should allow you to reach the hidden buttons.

That the same problem is present in kate isn't too surprising at all:
RKWard uses the same text editing component, and therefore some of the
same configuration pages. Likely it is one of those that is too large.

Could you please:

a) Post the installed version of the KDE libraries (Help->About
RKWard->Libraries)?
b) Click through the configuration pages (do not forget to also look
into tabs, where they exist), trying to identify whichever page
prevents shrinking? I.e. a page that is filled from top to bottom with
controls that cannot themselves be shrunk any further. (For instance,
scrollable view an typically shrink to around three or four rows of
text, but e.g. a checkbox control has a fixed height).

Regards
Thomas
